<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n433" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγέλαστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γελάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not laughing, grave, gloomy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				200
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρόσωπα βιαζόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					794
				</span></i>
			; of the orator Crassus, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Fin.</u>
				5.30
			</span></i>, cf. Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				75.11
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίβυλλα ἀγέλαστα φθεγγομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					92
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φρήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					290
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.Com.
					18
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πέτρα</span>, stone at Eleusis
			on which Demeter sat, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2587.183
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				1.5.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>not to be laughed at, not trifling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυμφοραί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			, v.l.
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.307
			</span></i>.</div>
